{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjxNkKirW46KcXH4xZvB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YMAdQMCTQLZwqU7CmLE5r4","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ../engine && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='crates/pav_tools/src/tools.rs'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('''    Tool {\n        name: \"spawn\",\n        help: \"Spawn a prop.\",''','''    Tool {\n        name: \"surgeon\",\n        help: \"Drive a surgery surgeon slot: aim, hold or press hands, pick a ring place, for N ticks.\",\n        args: &[\n            arg(\"slot\", \"integer\", \"surgeon slot 0-3 (default 0)\"),\n            arg(\"aim\", \"array\", \"[x, z] field position\"),\n            arg(\"hold\", \"string\", \"held: use,cancel,gift,precision,defib, comma separated\"),\n            arg(\"press\", \"string\", \"pressed on the first tick, same names\"),\n            arg(\"tool\", \"integer\", \"ring place 0-7 (0 = up, clockwise), or -1\"),\n            arg(\"pressure\", \"number\", \"analog pressure 0..1 (default 1)\"),\n            arg(\"rotate\", \"integer\", \"-1, 0 or 1: turn a held bone\"),\n            arg(\"cmd\", \"string\", \"a game command: advance, skip, retry\"),\n            arg(\"ticks\", \"integer\", \"ticks to run (default 1)\"),\n        ],\n        run: crate::play_tools::t_surgeon,\n    },\n    Tool {\n        name: \"case_check\",\n        help: \"Check surgery content: a case or story file by path, or everything: errors name the file and line.\",\n        args: &[arg(\"path\", \"string\", \"a content file to parse; omit to lint all the content\")],\n        run: crate::play_tools::t_case_check,\n    },\n    Tool {\n        name: \"balance\",\n        help: \"The surgery bot over seeds and skills: wins, time, vitals left and a suggested par per case.\",\n        args: &[\n            arg(\"seeds\", \"integer\", \"runs per skill per case (default 10)\"),\n            arg(\"skills\", \"string\", \"skills to try, comma separated (default 1.0,0.7,0.4)\"),\n            arg(\"case\", \"integer\", \"just this case (default all, 255 = Code Blue)\"),\n            arg(\"difficulty\", \"integer\", \"0 Resident, 1 Attending (default), 2 Chief\"),\n        ],\n        run: crate::play_tools::t_balance,\n    },\n    Tool {\n        name: \"spawn\",\n        help: \"Spawn a prop.\",''',1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='crates/pav_tools/src/play_tools.rs'\ns=open(p).read()\ns+='''\nfn hand_bits(a: &Args, key: &str) -> Result<u8> {\n    use pav_core::input::hands;\n    let Some(text) = crate::tools::get_str(a, key) else { return Ok(0) };\n    let mut bits = 0;\n    for n in text.split(',').map(str::trim).filter(|n| !n.is_empty()) {\n        bits |= match n {\n            \"use\" => hands::USE,\n            \"cancel\" => hands::CANCEL,\n            \"gift\" => hands::GIFT,\n            \"precision\" => hands::PRECISION,\n            \"defib\" => hands::DEFIB,\n            o => bail!(\"unknown hand '{o}' (use, cancel, gift, precision, defib)\"),\n        };\n    }\n    Ok(bits)\n}\n\n/// `surgeon`: drives one surgeon slot of the surgery game.\npub fn t_surgeon(s: &mut Session, a: &Args) -> Result<Output> {\n    use pav_core::InputFrame;\n    use pav_core::games::surgery::Surgery;\n    use pav_core::input::{SurgeonInput, SurgeryCmd};\n    let slot = get_u64(a, \"slot\", 0)? as usize;\n    if slot > 3 {\n        bail!(\"slot is 0-3\");\n    }\n    let (held, press) = (hand_bits(a, \"hold\")?, hand_bits(a, \"press\")?);\n    let n = get_u64(a, \"ticks\", 1)?.max(1);\n    let aim = crate::tools::vec_arg(a, \"aim\")?.filter(|v| v.len() == 2).map(|v| glam::Vec2::new(v[0], v[1]));\n    let tool = a.get(\"tool\").and_then(|v| v.as_i64()).unwrap_or(-1) as i8;\n    let pressure = a.get(\"pressure\").and_then(|v| v.as_f64()).unwrap_or(1.0) as f32;\n    let rotate = a.get(\"rotate\").and_then(|v| v.as_i64()).unwrap_or(0) as i8;\n    let cmd = match crate::tools::get_str(a, \"cmd\") {\n        Some(\"advance\") => Some(SurgeryCmd::Advance),\n        Some(\"skip\") => Some(SurgeryCmd::SkipScene),\n        Some(\"retry\") => Some(SurgeryCmd::Retry { from_start: false }),\n        Some(o) => bail!(\"unknown cmd '{o}' (advance, skip, retry)\"),\n        None => None,\n    };\n    if s.sim.play().and_then(|g| g.get::<Surgery>()).is_none() {\n        bail!(\"no surgery scene is running: `load scene=surgery/case/0`\");\n    }\n    for i in 0..n {\n        let was = s.sim.play().and_then(|g| g.get::<Surgery>()).map(|g| g.surgeons[slot].raw).unwrap_or_default();\n        let mut f = InputFrame::default();\n        f.surgeons[slot] = SurgeonInput {\n            active: true,\n            aim: aim.unwrap_or(was),\n            held: held | if i == 0 { press } else { 0 },\n            pressed: if i == 0 { press | held } else { 0 },\n            tool: if i == 0 { tool } else { -1 },\n            pressure,\n            assist: 0.0,\n            rotate,\n        };\n        if i == 0 {\n            f.surgery = cmd;\n        }\n        s.sim.step(&f);\n    }\n    s.keep_events();\n    s.sync_camera();\n    let g = s.sim.play().expect(\"the game is still running\");\n    Ok(Output::Json(json!({ \"status\": g.status(&s.sim) })))\n}\n\n/// `case_check`: parses one content file, or lints them all.\npub fn t_case_check(_: &mut Session, a: &Args) -> Result<Output> {\n    use pav_core::games::surgery::content::{CaseDef, Content, StoryDef};\n    if let Some(path) = crate::tools::get_str(a, \"path\") {\n        let text = std::fs::read_to_string(path).map_err(|e| anyhow::anyhow!(\"{path}: {e}\"))?;\n        let parsed = if path.contains(\"story\") {\n            toml::from_str::<StoryDef>(&text).map(|_| ()).map_err(|e| e.to_string())\n        } else {\n            toml::from_str::<CaseDef>(&text).map(|_| ()).map_err(|e| e.to_string())\n        };\n        return Ok(Output::Json(match parsed {\n            Ok(()) => json!({ \"path\": path, \"ok\": true }),\n            Err(e) => json!({ \"path\": path, \"ok\": false, \"error\": e }),\n        }));\n    }\n    let c = Content::read()?;\n    let problems = c.lint();\n    Ok(Output::Json(json!({ \"ok\": problems.is_empty(), \"problems\": problems, \"cases\": c.cases.len(), \"stories\": c.stories.len() })))\n}\n\n/// `balance`: the bot over seeds and skills, per case.\npub fn t_balance(_: &mut Session, a: &Args) -> Result<Output> {\n    use pav_core::games::surgery::content::{self, CODE_BLUE};\n    use pav_core::games::surgery::Surgery;\n    let seeds = get_u64(a, \"seeds\", 10)?.clamp(1, 200);\n    let text = crate::tools::get_str(a, \"skills\").unwrap_or(\"1.0,0.7,0.4\").to_string();\n    let diff = get_u64(a, \"difficulty\", 1)? as u8;\n    let skills: Vec<f32> = text.split(',').filter_map(|s| s.trim().parse().ok()).collect();\n    let cases: Vec<u8> = match a.get(\"case\").and_then(|v| v.as_u64()) {\n        Some(c) => vec![c as u8],\n        None => (0..content::CASES as u8).chain([CODE_BLUE]).collect(),\n    };\n    let mut rows = Vec::new();\n    for case in cases {\n        let scene = if case == CODE_BLUE { \"surgery/codeblue\".to_string() } else { format!(\"surgery/case/{case}\") };\n        let name = content::get().case(case).map(|c| c.name.clone()).unwrap_or_default();\n        let mut per_skill = Vec::new();\n        for skill in &skills {\n            let (mut wins, mut time, mut vitals, mut score, mut codes) = (0u32, 0.0f32, 0.0f32, 0i64, 0u32);\n            let mut ranks = std::collections::BTreeMap::new();\n            for seed in 1..=seeds {\n                let mut sim = Sim::new(&scene, seed)?;\n                {\n                    let g = sim.state.play.as_mut().and_then(|g| g.get_mut::<Surgery>()).expect(\"a surgery game\");\n                    g.bot_skill = *skill;\n                }\n                sim.step(&pav_core::InputFrame {\n                    surgery: Some(pav_core::input::SurgeryCmd::Difficulty(diff)),\n                    ..Default::default()\n                });\n                let (o, t) = sim.run_bot(60 * 60 * 30);\n                let g = sim.play().and_then(|g| g.get::<Surgery>()).expect(\"a surgery game\");\n                if o == Outcome::Won {\n                    wins += 1;\n                    if let Some(r) = &g.results {\n                        *ranks.entry(r.rank.to_string()).or_insert(0u32) += 1;\n                        score += r.total as i64;\n                    }\n                    vitals += g.op.vitals;\n                }\n                time += t as f32 / 60.0;\n                codes += g.op.counters.notes.get(\"code\").copied().unwrap_or(0);\n            }\n            let n = seeds as f32;\n            per_skill.push(json!({\n                \"skill\": skill,\n                \"wins\": format!(\"{wins}/{seeds}\"),\n                \"seconds\": (time / n).round(),\n                \"vitals_left\": if wins > 0 { (vitals / wins as f32).round() } else { 0.0 },\n                \"avg_score\": if wins > 0 { score / wins as i64 } else { 0 },\n                \"codes\": codes,\n                \"ranks\": ranks,\n            }));\n        }\n        // The par that puts skill 1.0 at the top of S.\n        let suggested = per_skill.first().and_then(|r| r[\"avg_score\"].as_i64()).unwrap_or(0) as f32 / 1.08;\n        rows.push(json!({ \"case\": case, \"name\": name, \"suggested_par\": (suggested / 100.0).round() * 100.0, \"runs\": per_skill }));\n    }\n    Ok(Output::Json(json!({ \"balance\": rows })))\n}\n'''\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"^use\\|fn get_str\\|fn vec_arg\" crates/pav_tools/src/play_tools.rs crates/pav_tools/src/tools.rs | head -14; grep -n \"toml\" crates/pav_tools/Cargo.toml | head -2; cat > crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/content/README.md <<'EOF'\n# Making more of this game\n\nEverything a designer touches is a text file in this folder. Running from the repository root,\n`pav` and the window read these files at each load (dev mode has **Reload content**), so edits need\nno rebuild. A new file also needs one line in `content.rs`'s `FILES`, so it is embedded for the\nbrowser; a test fails if you forget.\n\nCheck your work: `pav case_check` lints everything (every error names the file and line),\n`pav case_check path=<file>` parses one, and `pav balance case=<n>` runs the bot over seeds.\n\n## Add a case\nCopy `cases/case0.toml`. The top sets the `surgeon` (`mara`, `pet`, `both`), `plate`, the eight\ninstruments of the `ring` (clockwise from up), `timer` in seconds, `par` (the score ranks are\npercentages of: take it from `pav balance`), the patient's chart and `fate` lines, and the `before`\nand `after` story scenes. `guided = true` highlights targets; `gift = true` wakes the gift at once.\n\nEach `[[phase]]` has an `objective` (the NOW line), `checkpoint = true` if a death retries from here,\n`plate` to cross-fade to, `meter` for the monitor, a `strain`, a list of `[[phase.spawn]]` and a list of\n`[[phase.event]]`. A phase ends when every required hazard and the strain are gone.\n\n- Spawn kinds: `incision laceration pool bleeder foreign polyp tumor burn bone nodule sac crown eye ember\n  tether tendril closure furnace`. Lines take `pts`, things take `at`, `r`, `axis` (degrees, the pull),\n  `tag` (`hook shard splinter ember cyst inflammation seed`), `hidden = true` (needs the Scanner),\n  `optional = true` (doesn't hold the phase up). A `bone` has `to` (its home) and `angle` (how it starts).\n- Triggers on an event: `at_time`, `vitals_below`, `on_beat`, `remaining` (tasks left), `on_clear`.\n- What it does: `spawn`, `say = [speaker, line]`, `cue`, `banner`, `code = true` (a scripted stop),\n  `shake`, `plate`, `gift = true`, `vitals`, `push` (camera).\n\nAdd the case to the campaign by numbering it next and raising `CASES` in `content.rs`.\n\n## Add a strain\nA strain is a state machine in `strain/<name>.rs` with its numbers in data\n(`strain = { kind = \"...\", waves = 3, count = 6, beats = 12, ... }`). Implement start, tick and killed, add\nit to `StrainKind` in `strain/mod.rs`, and teach the bot if it needs a new gesture (`bot.rs`).\n\n## Add a line of dialogue\nStory files are `[[line]]` lists: `who`, `expr`, `text`, plus stage commands on the same or their own line:\n`set`, `enter` with `at` (`left right centre farleft farright`), `exit` (a name, or `all`), `music` (`tender`\n`tense` `title`), `cue`, `camera` (`paper`, `or`), `flash`, `shake`. Write it deadly serious. In-op callouts are in\n`callouts.toml` by trigger; `nurse` means whoever is calling the operation.\n\n## Add a character\nCopy `rigs/mara.toml`. `pitch`, `wave`, `pace` and `jitter` are the voice. `palette` names the colours. Each\n`[[part]]` is a closed outline, layered by `z` (back hair 0, shoulders 1, face 3, eyes 3.6 to 4.4, front hair\n5), with `chaikin` rounding, `mirror`, a `role` (`brow lid eye iris pupil hair head`) and `spring` for hair.\nEvery character needs the four expressions `neutral alarmed stern soft`: brow moves, lids, irises, and\nthe mouth's `closed` and `open` shapes. `pav case_check` says what's missing.\n\n## Add a plate or a set\nA plate (`plates/*.toml`) is `lobes` (`x, z, a, b, h`: ellipses of tissue), a palette, `pulse` and `breathe`,\n`veins`, `vessels` and `ridges` as polylines. A set (`sets/*.toml`) is cards: `[[layer]]` with `z` behind the\nstage, `color`, `points`, `chaikin`, `emissive`, `monitor = true` for a live trace, `repeat = [count, spacing]`, and\n`rain = true`.\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\np='crates/pav_tools/src/tools.rs'\ns=open(p).read()\nimport re\nprint(re.findall(r'(?:pub )?fn (?:get_str|vec_arg|get_u64|get_bool)[^\\n]*', s))\nEOF\nsed -i 's/^fn vec_arg/pub(crate) fn vec_arg/' crates/pav_tools/src/tools.rs; CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=12 cargo build --offline -p pav_tools --bin pav 2>&1 | grep -E \"^error|^ +--> \" -A4 | head -40; ./target/debug/pav case_check | cut -c1-500; time ./target/debug/pav balance seeds=4 skills=1.0,0.7,0.4,0 2>&1 | python3 -c \"\nimport json,sys\nd=json.load(sys.stdin)\nfor c in d['balance']:\n    print(c['case'],c['name'],'par',c['suggested_par'])\n    for r in c['runs']:\n        print('   ',r['skill'],r['wins'],'t',r['seconds'],'v',r['vitals_left'],'score',r['avg_score'],'codes',r['codes'],r['ranks'])\n\"","description":"Add the case_check, balance and surgeon tools, then run the balance","timeout":590000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3930,"cache_read_input_tokens":686598,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3930},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"092dc2e9-85ec-49f9-8a5e-82413bbc454c","uuid":"7e19b116-0817-4a2d-9bdd-18de2c97d2c7","timestamp":"2026-11-05T14:41:53.175Z","request_id":"req_011CgjxNjztGxcbZ7hXFfpVB","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01YMAdQMCTQLZwqU7CmLE5r4":{"command":"cd ../engine && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='crates/pav_tools/src/tools.rs'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('''    Tool {\n        name: \"spawn\",\n        help: \"Spawn a prop.\",''','''    Tool {\n        name: \"surgeon\",\n        help: \"Drive a surgery surgeon slot: aim, hold or press hands, pick a ring place, for N ticks.\",\n        args: &[\n            arg(\"slot\", \"integer\", \"surgeon slot 0-3 (default 0)\"),\n            arg(\"aim\", \"array\", \"[x, z] field position\"),\n            arg(\"hold\", \"string\", \"held: use,cancel,gift,precision,defib, comma separated\"),\n            arg(\"press\", \"string\", \"pressed on the first tick, same names\"),\n            arg(\"tool\", \"integer\", \"ring place 0-7 (0 = up, clockwise), or -1\"),\n            arg(\"pressure\", \"number\", \"analog pressure 0..1 (default 1)\"),\n            arg(\"rotate\", \"integer\", \"-1, 0 or 1: turn a held bone\"),\n            arg(\"cmd\", \"string\", \"a game command: advance, skip, retry\"),\n            arg(\"ticks\", \"integer\", \"ticks to run (default 1)\"),\n        ],\n        run: crate::play_tools::t_surgeon,\n    },\n    Tool {\n        name: \"case_check\",\n        help: \"Check surgery content: a case or story file by path, or everything: errors name the file and line.\",\n        args: &[arg(\"path\", \"string\", \"a content file to parse; omit to lint all the content\")],\n        run: crate::play_tools::t_case_check,\n    },\n    Tool {\n        name: \"balance\",\n        help: \"The surgery bot over seeds and skills: wins, time, vitals left and a suggested par per case.\",\n        args: &[\n            arg(\"seeds\", \"integer\", \"runs per skill per case (default 10)\"),\n            arg(\"skills\", \"string\", \"skills to try, comma separated (default 1.0,0.7,0.4)\"),\n            arg(\"case\", \"integer\", \"just this case (default all, 255 = Code Blue)\"),\n            arg(\"difficulty\", \"integer\", \"0 Resident, 1 Attending (default), 2 Chief\"),\n        ],\n        run: crate::play_tools::t_balance,\n    },\n    Tool {\n        name: \"spawn\",\n        help: \"Spawn a prop.\",''',1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='crates/pav_tools/src/play_tools.rs'\ns=open(p).read()\ns+='''\nfn hand_bits(a: &Args, key: &str) -> Result<u8> {\n    use pav_core::input::hands;\n    let Some(text) = crate::tools::get_str(a, key) else { return Ok(0) };\n    let mut bits = 0;\n    for n in text.split(',').map(str::trim).filter(|n| !n.is_empty()) {\n        bits |= match n {\n            \"use\" => hands::USE,\n            \"cancel\" => hands::CANCEL,\n            \"gift\" => hands::GIFT,\n            \"precision\" => hands::PRECISION,\n            \"defib\" => hands::DEFIB,\n            o => bail!(\"unknown hand '{o}' (use, cancel, gift, precision, defib)\"),\n        };\n    }\n    Ok(bits)\n}\n\n/// `surgeon`: drives one surgeon slot of the surgery game.\npub fn t_surgeon(s: &mut Session, a: &Args) -> Result<Output> {\n    use pav_core::InputFrame;\n    use pav_core::games::surgery::Surgery;\n    use pav_core::input::{SurgeonInput, SurgeryCmd};\n    let slot = get_u64(a, \"slot\", 0)? as usize;\n    if slot > 3 {\n        bail!(\"slot is 0-3\");\n    }\n    let (held, press) = (hand_bits(a, \"hold\")?, hand_bits(a, \"press\")?);\n    let n = get_u64(a, \"ticks\", 1)?.max(1);\n    let aim = crate::tools::vec_arg(a, \"aim\")?.filter(|v| v.len() == 2).map(|v| glam::Vec2::new(v[0], v[1]));\n    let tool = a.get(\"tool\").and_then(|v| v.as_i64()).unwrap_or(-1) as i8;\n    let pressure = a.get(\"pressure\").and_then(|v| v.as_f64()).unwrap_or(1.0) as f32;\n    let rotate = a.get(\"rotate\").and_then(|v| v.as_i64()).unwrap_or(0) as i8;\n    let cmd = match crate::tools::get_str(a, \"cmd\") {\n        Some(\"advance\") => Some(SurgeryCmd::Advance),\n        Some(\"skip\") => Some(SurgeryCmd::SkipScene),\n        Some(\"retry\") => Some(SurgeryCmd::Retry { from_start: false }),\n        Some(o) => bail!(\"unknown cmd '{o}' (advance, skip, retry)\"),\n        None => None,\n    };\n    if s.sim.play().and_then(|g| g.get::<Surgery>()).is_none() {\n        bail!(\"no surgery scene is running: `load scene=surgery/case/0`\");\n    }\n    for i in 0..n {\n        let was = s.sim.play().and_then(|g| g.get::<Surgery>()).map(|g| g.surgeons[slot].raw).unwrap_or_default();\n        let mut f = InputFrame::default();\n        f.surgeons[slot] = SurgeonInput {\n            active: true,\n            aim: aim.unwrap_or(was),\n            held: held | if i == 0 { press } else { 0 },\n            pressed: if i == 0 { press | held } else { 0 },\n            tool: if i == 0 { tool } else { -1 },\n            pressure,\n            assist: 0.0,\n            rotate,\n        };\n        if i == 0 {\n            f.surgery = cmd;\n        }\n        s.sim.step(&f);\n    }\n    s.keep_events();\n    s.sync_camera();\n    let g = s.sim.play().expect(\"the game is still running\");\n    Ok(Output::Json(json!({ \"status\": g.status(&s.sim) })))\n}\n\n/// `case_check`: parses one content file, or lints them all.\npub fn t_case_check(_: &mut Session, a: &Args) -> Result<Output> {\n    use pav_core::games::surgery::content::{CaseDef, Content, StoryDef};\n    if let Some(path) = crate::tools::get_str(a, \"path\") {\n        let text = std::fs::read_to_string(path).map_err(|e| anyhow::anyhow!(\"{path}: {e}\"))?;\n        let parsed = if path.contains(\"story\") {\n            toml::from_str::<StoryDef>(&text).map(|_| ()).map_err(|e| e.to_string())\n        } else {\n            toml::from_str::<CaseDef>(&text).map(|_| ()).map_err(|e| e.to_string())\n        };\n        return Ok(Output::Json(match parsed {\n            Ok(()) => json!({ \"path\": path, \"ok\": true }),\n            Err(e) => json!({ \"path\": path, \"ok\": false, \"error\": e }),\n        }));\n    }\n    let c = Content::read()?;\n    let problems = c.lint();\n    Ok(Output::Json(json!({ \"ok\": problems.is_empty(), \"problems\": problems, \"cases\": c.cases.len(), \"stories\": c.stories.len() })))\n}\n\n/// `balance`: the bot over seeds and skills, per case.\npub fn t_balance(_: &mut Session, a: &Args) -> Result<Output> {\n    use pav_core::games::surgery::content::{self, CODE_BLUE};\n    use pav_core::games::surgery::Surgery;\n    let seeds = get_u64(a, \"seeds\", 10)?.clamp(1, 200);\n    let text = crate::tools::get_str(a, \"skills\").unwrap_or(\"1.0,0.7,0.4\").to_string();\n    let diff = get_u64(a, \"difficulty\", 1)? as u8;\n    let skills: Vec<f32> = text.split(',').filter_map(|s| s.trim().parse().ok()).collect();\n    let cases: Vec<u8> = match a.get(\"case\").and_then(|v| v.as_u64()) {\n        Some(c) => vec![c as u8],\n        None => (0..content::CASES as u8).chain([CODE_BLUE]).collect(),\n    };\n    let mut rows = Vec::new();\n    for case in cases {\n        let scene = if case == CODE_BLUE { \"surgery/codeblue\".to_string() } else { format!(\"surgery/case/{case}\") };\n        let name = content::get().case(case).map(|c| c.name.clone()).unwrap_or_default();\n        let mut per_skill = Vec::new();\n        for skill in &skills {\n            let (mut wins, mut time, mut vitals, mut score, mut codes) = (0u32, 0.0f32, 0.0f32, 0i64, 0u32);\n            let mut ranks = std::collections::BTreeMap::new();\n            for seed in 1..=seeds {\n                let mut sim = Sim::new(&scene, seed)?;\n                {\n                    let g = sim.state.play.as_mut().and_then(|g| g.get_mut::<Surgery>()).expect(\"a surgery game\");\n                    g.bot_skill = *skill;\n                }\n                sim.step(&pav_core::InputFrame {\n                    surgery: Some(pav_core::input::SurgeryCmd::Difficulty(diff)),\n                    ..Default::default()\n                });\n                let (o, t) = sim.run_bot(60 * 60 * 30);\n                let g = sim.play().and_then(|g| g.get::<Surgery>()).expect(\"a surgery game\");\n                if o == Outcome::Won {\n                    wins += 1;\n                    if let Some(r) = &g.results {\n                        *ranks.entry(r.rank.to_string()).or_insert(0u32) += 1;\n                        score += r.total as i64;\n                    }\n                    vitals += g.op.vitals;\n                }\n                time += t as f32 / 60.0;\n                codes += g.op.counters.notes.get(\"code\").copied().unwrap_or(0);\n            }\n            let n = seeds as f32;\n            per_skill.push(json!({\n                \"skill\": skill,\n                \"wins\": format!(\"{wins}/{seeds}\"),\n                \"seconds\": (time / n).round(),\n                \"vitals_left\": if wins > 0 { (vitals / wins as f32).round() } else { 0.0 },\n                \"avg_score\": if wins > 0 { score / wins as i64 } else { 0 },\n                \"codes\": codes,\n                \"ranks\": ranks,\n            }));\n        }\n        // The par that puts skill 1.0 at the top of S.\n        let suggested = per_skill.first().and_then(|r| r[\"avg_score\"].as_i64()).unwrap_or(0) as f32 / 1.08;\n        rows.push(json!({ \"case\": case, \"name\": name, \"suggested_par\": (suggested / 100.0).round() * 100.0, \"runs\": per_skill }));\n    }\n    Ok(Output::Json(json!({ \"balance\": rows })))\n}\n'''\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"^use\\|fn get_str\\|fn vec_arg\" crates/pav_tools/src/play_tools.rs crates/pav_tools/src/tools.rs | head -14; grep -n \"toml\" crates/pav_tools/Cargo.toml | head -2; cat > crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/content/README.md <<'EOF'\n# Making more of this game\n\nEverything a designer touches is a text file in this folder. Running from the repository root,\n`pav` and the window read these files at each load (dev mode has **Reload content**), so edits need\nno rebuild. A new file also needs one line in `content.rs`'s `FILES`, so it is embedded for the\nbrowser; a test fails if you forget.\n\nCheck your work: `pav case_check` lints everything (every error names the file and line),\n`pav case_check path=<file>` parses one, and `pav balance case=<n>` runs the bot over seeds.\n\n## Add a case\nCopy `cases/case0.toml`. The top sets the `surgeon` (`mara`, `pet`, `both`), `plate`, the eight\ninstruments of the `ring` (clockwise from up), `timer` in seconds, `par` (the score ranks are\npercentages of: take it from `pav balance`), the patient's chart and `fate` lines, and the `before`\nand `after` story scenes. `guided = true` highlights targets; `gift = true` wakes the gift at once.\n\nEach `[[phase]]` has an `objective` (the NOW line), `checkpoint = true` if a death retries from here,\n`plate` to cross-fade to, `meter` for the monitor, a `strain`, a list of `[[phase.spawn]]` and a list of\n`[[phase.event]]`. A phase ends when every required hazard and the strain are gone.\n\n- Spawn kinds: `incision laceration pool bleeder foreign polyp tumor burn bone nodule sac crown eye ember\n  tether tendril closure furnace`. Lines take `pts`, things take `at`, `r`, `axis` (degrees, the pull),\n  `tag` (`hook shard splinter ember cyst inflammation seed`), `hidden = true` (needs the Scanner),\n  `optional = true` (doesn't hold the phase up). A `bone` has `to` (its home) and `angle` (how it starts).\n- Triggers on an event: `at_time`, `vitals_below`, `on_beat`, `remaining` (tasks left), `on_clear`.\n- What it does: `spawn`, `say = [speaker, line]`, `cue`, `banner`, `code = true` (a scripted stop),\n  `shake`, `plate`, `gift = true`, `vitals`, `push` (camera).\n\nAdd the case to the campaign by numbering it next and raising `CASES` in `content.rs`.\n\n## Add a strain\nA strain is a state machine in `strain/<name>.rs` with its numbers in data\n(`strain = { kind = \"...\", waves = 3, count = 6, beats = 12, ... }`). Implement start, tick and killed, add\nit to `StrainKind` in `strain/mod.rs`, and teach the bot if it needs a new gesture (`bot.rs`).\n\n## Add a line of dialogue\nStory files are `[[line]]` lists: `who`, `expr`, `text`, plus stage commands on the same or their own line:\n`set`, `enter` with `at` (`left right centre farleft farright`), `exit` (a name, or `all`), `music` (`tender`\n`tense` `title`), `cue`, `camera` (`paper`, `or`), `flash`, `shake`. Write it deadly serious. In-op callouts are in\n`callouts.toml` by trigger; `nurse` means whoever is calling the operation.\n\n## Add a character\nCopy `rigs/mara.toml`. `pitch`, `wave`, `pace` and `jitter` are the voice. `palette` names the colours. Each\n`[[part]]` is a closed outline, layered by `z` (back hair 0, shoulders 1, face 3, eyes 3.6 to 4.4, front hair\n5), with `chaikin` rounding, `mirror`, a `role` (`brow lid eye iris pupil hair head`) and `spring` for hair.\nEvery character needs the four expressions `neutral alarmed stern soft`: brow moves, lids, irises, and\nthe mouth's `closed` and `open` shapes. `pav case_check` says what's missing.\n\n## Add a plate or a set\nA plate (`plates/*.toml`) is `lobes` (`x, z, a, b, h`: ellipses of tissue), a palette, `pulse` and `breathe`,\n`veins`, `vessels` and `ridges` as polylines. A set (`sets/*.toml`) is cards: `[[layer]]` with `z` behind the\nstage, `color`, `points`, `chaikin`, `emissive`, `monitor = true` for a live trace, `repeat = [count, spacing]`, and\n`rain = true`.\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\np='crates/pav_tools/src/tools.rs'\ns=open(p).read()\nimport re\nprint(re.findall(r'(?:pub )?fn (?:get_str|vec_arg|get_u64|get_bool)[^\\n]*', s))\nEOF\nsed -i 's/^fn vec_arg/pub(crate) fn vec_arg/' crates/pav_tools/src/tools.rs; CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=12 cargo build --offline -p pav_tools --bin pav 2>&1 | grep -E \"^error|^ +--> \" -A4 | head -40; ./target/debug/pav case_check | cut -c1-500; time ./target/debug/pav balance seeds=4 skills=1.0,0.7,0.4,0 2>&1 | python3 -c \"\nimport json,sys\nd=json.load(sys.stdin)\nfor c in d['balance']:\n    print(c['case'],c['name'],'par',c['suggested_par'])\n    for r in c['runs']:\n        print('   ',r['skill'],r['wins'],'t',r['seconds'],'v',r['vitals_left'],'score',r['avg_score'],'codes',r['codes'],r['ranks'])\n\"","description":"Add the case_check, balance and surgeon tools, then run the balance","timeout":590000}}}
