{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015nJCbpHfsmLZq7ogQRD6Du","type":"tool_result","content":"warning: fields `steps` and `bot` are never read\n21 | pub struct Hook {\n22 |     pub steps: u64,\n   |         ^^^^^\n23 |     pub bot: bool,\n   |         ^^^\nwarning: fields `first_frame` and `last` are never read\n29 | pub struct Hub {\n40 |     pub first_frame: bool,\n   |         ^^^^^^^^^^^\n51 |     pub last: Option<std::time::Duration>,\n   |         ^^^^\nwarning: `pav_app` (bin \"shardfall\") generated 2 warnings","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"092dc2e9-85ec-49f9-8a5e-82413bbc454c","uuid":"3b48671f-2a2a-45ac-9024-353431bab6bb","timestamp":"2026-11-05T16:50:40.390Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"warning: fields `steps` and `bot` are never read\n21 | pub struct Hook {\n22 |     pub steps: u64,\n   |         ^^^^^\n23 |     pub bot: bool,\n   |         ^^^\nwarning: fields `first_frame` and `last` are never read\n29 | pub struct Hub {\n40 |     pub first_frame: bool,\n   |         ^^^^^^^^^^^\n51 |     pub last: Option<std::time::Duration>,\n   |         ^^^^\nwarning: `pav_app` (bin \"shardfall\") generated 2 warnings","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_015nJCbpHfsmLZq7ogQRD6Du","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgk8GFcp5V16LkVRaSay5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now the final feedback text, based on what actually happened in this run."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":532,"cache_read_input_tokens":897173,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":532},"output_tokens":41,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"092dc2e9-85ec-49f9-8a5e-82413bbc454c","uuid":"6cd862ef-b825-4416-a754-156ac0df15e0","timestamp":"2026-11-05T16:50:41.789Z","request_id":"req_011Cgk8GFGz78fLNJJUiJXeX"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgk8GFcp5V16LkVRaSay5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FLLyNf7u8nqvipmpqN1M5R","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='crates/pav_app/src/hub.rs'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('''pub struct Hook {\n    pub steps: u64,\n    pub bot: bool,\n    pub installed: bool,\n}''','''pub struct Hook {\n    pub installed: bool,\n}''')\ns=s.replace('''    pub first_frame: bool,\n''','').replace('''    pub last: Option<std::time::Duration>,\n''','')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nimport json\np='../../exit-interview.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nd['testingFeedback']=[\n \"About 30. The ones that mattered: the tumor's ring cut was never spawned, so Case 3 could not be finished; the closing dressing locked out the IV, so a low-vitals player was stuck until death; touch taps missed the Settings button because the canvas was not sized the way the pointer events assumed; slow frames kept hub copies from calling ready in time; the title clipped on a phone; the attract timer ran slow on slow frames; menu repeats overshot on stalled frames; the campaign never used the IV; glasses hid the eyes; the wide-shot camera sat behind a wall; plus a dozen balance and test-harness fixes.\",\n \"4: the unfinishable Case 3 tumor, the dressing lock, phone taps missing the only button on that screen, and four-player hub rounds failing the harness.\",\n \"The bot playing every case and the whole campaign with coverage counters, together with the balance tool. It runs in seconds, found the unfinishable case and the dressing lock, and told me what to change after every rule edit.\",\n \"Browser tests that waited on real time before I made them count frames: software WebGPU on this busy machine ran at about 1 to 10 frames a second, so they mostly measured the machine. The WebKit iPhone load also told me little, because it stops at the page's WebGPU message.\"\n]\nd['engineFeedback']=[\n \"Everything runs and draws headless. A deterministic sim behind one small hook, `pav capture` for a real frame in about a second, and `DynamicMesh` plus SDF solids meant I could paint a whole beating organ and see it without a display.\",\n \"Yes, in small ways. Leftover events from the last scene turned into wild distortions in my first captures, which looked like a rendering bug. I guessed the story camera's distance and put it behind a wall. A new dependency needs one build without --locked. And big release compiles were killed for memory on this shared machine until I built with fewer jobs from a script that waits for free memory.\",\n \"The game's own frame path and shell in product.rs and pav_ui: focus-list menus, prompts that follow the device, per-pad input with analog triggers, the HUD, and the hub bridge. The plate renderer and the bus mixer with its sequencer and formant voices came next.\",\n \"Getting out of the demo's way. App::frame carries about 800 lines of demo behaviour, and there is no per-game camera, sound or UI seam, so a game that wants its own screens has to branch above all of it and reopen several crates.\",\n \"input.rs: surgeon slots and a game command in InputFrame, for replays and co-op. frame.rs and sim.rs: a Cue event and a per-game frame, because the hook cannot draw. build.rs: a per-game emit at the end of the build. session.rs and headless.rs: the game's camera and shell, so the tools see what the window sees. pav_audio: three buses, formant filters, vibrato, a raised voice limit, cues, music and voices. app.rs, simhost.rs and settings.rs: a branch to the game's own frame path and a command queue. pack_single_html.py and index.html: the hub client, tags, shim and About block.\",\n \"Give games a real seam for their own frame: a trait with camera, draw, sound and UI hooks that the window and the headless tools both call, with the demo's behaviour living behind it instead of in App::frame.\"\n]\nd['promptFeedback']=[\n \"The plan's check marks. Knowing which values, look and protocol shape had already been tried on this machine saved a great deal of searching, and the plan's clear Never cut list made every trade-off easy.\",\n \"Mostly small things: the task lets me pick genre and perspective while the plan fixes them, and the plan says it never names the deliverable while its build line needs one. The first was settled by the plan's own note that the task's requirements win.\",\n \"Passing the hub harness with four software-rendered copies on a shared machine with little free memory, because the protocol's deadlines do not wait for slow frames. The sheer breadth was the other: a whole game, engine seams, audio, co-op and tools in one run.\",\n \"State a memory budget for builds and browsers alongside the port rules, since other agents compete for it. And say whether a hub round must pass on software rendering, because that drove real design decisions such as the keepalive and the draw throttle.\"\n]\njson.dump(d,open(p,'w'),ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)\nEOF\npython3 -c \"import json;d=json.load(open('../../exit-interview.json'));print(len(d['testingFeedback']),len(d['engineFeedback']),len(d['promptFeedback']),d['aiHub']['players'])\"; python3 ../gen/about.py; python3 -c \"import json;print([ (s['title'],len(s['lines'])) for s in json.load(open('web/about.json'))['sections']])\"; timeout 570 ../tests/build_page.sh 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-110","description":"Write the final feedback, generate the About block and rebuild","timeout":590000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":532,"cache_read_input_tokens":897173,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":532},"output_tokens":41,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"092dc2e9-85ec-49f9-8a5e-82413bbc454c","uuid":"63a4230f-a0b2-477f-9d2c-b2f49ea44645","timestamp":"2026-11-05T16:51:00.402Z","request_id":"req_011Cgk8GFGz78fLNJJUiJXeX","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01FLLyNf7u8nqvipmpqN1M5R":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='crates/pav_app/src/hub.rs'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('''pub struct Hook {\n    pub steps: u64,\n    pub bot: bool,\n    pub installed: bool,\n}''','''pub struct Hook {\n    pub installed: bool,\n}''')\ns=s.replace('''    pub first_frame: bool,\n''','').replace('''    pub last: Option<std::time::Duration>,\n''','')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nimport json\np='../../exit-interview.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nd['testingFeedback']=[\n \"About 30. The ones that mattered: the tumor's ring cut was never spawned, so Case 3 could not be finished; the closing dressing locked out the IV, so a low-vitals player was stuck until death; touch taps missed the Settings button because the canvas was not sized the way the pointer events assumed; slow frames kept hub copies from calling ready in time; the title clipped on a phone; the attract timer ran slow on slow frames; menu repeats overshot on stalled frames; the campaign never used the IV; glasses hid the eyes; the wide-shot camera sat behind a wall; plus a dozen balance and test-harness fixes.\",\n \"4: the unfinishable Case 3 tumor, the dressing lock, phone taps missing the only button on that screen, and four-player hub rounds failing the harness.\",\n \"The bot playing every case and the whole campaign with coverage counters, together with the balance tool. It runs in seconds, found the unfinishable case and the dressing lock, and told me what to change after every rule edit.\",\n \"Browser tests that waited on real time before I made them count frames: software WebGPU on this busy machine ran at about 1 to 10 frames a second, so they mostly measured the machine. The WebKit iPhone load also told me little, because it stops at the page's WebGPU message.\"\n]\nd['engineFeedback']=[\n \"Everything runs and draws headless. A deterministic sim behind one small hook, `pav capture` for a real frame in about a second, and `DynamicMesh` plus SDF solids meant I could paint a whole beating organ and see it without a display.\",\n \"Yes, in small ways. Leftover events from the last scene turned into wild distortions in my first captures, which looked like a rendering bug. I guessed the story camera's distance and put it behind a wall. A new dependency needs one build without --locked. And big release compiles were killed for memory on this shared machine until I built with fewer jobs from a script that waits for free memory.\",\n \"The game's own frame path and shell in product.rs and pav_ui: focus-list menus, prompts that follow the device, per-pad input with analog triggers, the HUD, and the hub bridge. The plate renderer and the bus mixer with its sequencer and formant voices came next.\",\n \"Getting out of the demo's way. App::frame carries about 800 lines of demo behaviour, and there is no per-game camera, sound or UI seam, so a game that wants its own screens has to branch above all of it and reopen several crates.\",\n \"input.rs: surgeon slots and a game command in InputFrame, for replays and co-op. frame.rs and sim.rs: a Cue event and a per-game frame, because the hook cannot draw. build.rs: a per-game emit at the end of the build. session.rs and headless.rs: the game's camera and shell, so the tools see what the window sees. pav_audio: three buses, formant filters, vibrato, a raised voice limit, cues, music and voices. app.rs, simhost.rs and settings.rs: a branch to the game's own frame path and a command queue. pack_single_html.py and index.html: the hub client, tags, shim and About block.\",\n \"Give games a real seam for their own frame: a trait with camera, draw, sound and UI hooks that the window and the headless tools both call, with the demo's behaviour living behind it instead of in App::frame.\"\n]\nd['promptFeedback']=[\n \"The plan's check marks. Knowing which values, look and protocol shape had already been tried on this machine saved a great deal of searching, and the plan's clear Never cut list made every trade-off easy.\",\n \"Mostly small things: the task lets me pick genre and perspective while the plan fixes them, and the plan says it never names the deliverable while its build line needs one. The first was settled by the plan's own note that the task's requirements win.\",\n \"Passing the hub harness with four software-rendered copies on a shared machine with little free memory, because the protocol's deadlines do not wait for slow frames. The sheer breadth was the other: a whole game, engine seams, audio, co-op and tools in one run.\",\n \"State a memory budget for builds and browsers alongside the port rules, since other agents compete for it. And say whether a hub round must pass on software rendering, because that drove real design decisions such as the keepalive and the draw throttle.\"\n]\njson.dump(d,open(p,'w'),ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)\nEOF\npython3 -c \"import json;d=json.load(open('../../exit-interview.json'));print(len(d['testingFeedback']),len(d['engineFeedback']),len(d['promptFeedback']),d['aiHub']['players'])\"; python3 ../gen/about.py; python3 -c \"import json;print([ (s['title'],len(s['lines'])) for s in json.load(open('web/about.json'))['sections']])\"; timeout 570 ../tests/build_page.sh 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-110","description":"Write the final feedback, generate the About block and rebuild","timeout":590000}}}
