{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Bash, Monitor, Read, TaskStop, ToolSearch, Write</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user set a goal via `/goal`: \"Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says. Done when: Everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer is done, and everything TASK.md asks you to hand in is in this folder.\"\n   - STAGE.md: \"Build the game PLAN.md describes. Take your file names and what to hand in from TASK.md, which is filled in for you. Keep your progress in PROGRESS.md, so you can pick up where you were after your context is compacted.\"\n   - TASK.md: SOURCE Trauma Center: Second Opinion; title a playful riff picked by real RNG from 50 silently brainstormed; one HTML named `[GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-063049].html` in root; dev files in a subfolder of the same name; build on the shardfall/Pavilion engine; all audio in code, music default 10%, Animalese-style voices; AI Hub multiplayer; attract mode at 10 s idle; dev mode from pause with live sliders and reset; 10-foot controller-first UX with native keyboard/mouse, prompts following last device, Xbox glyph setting; touch-only shows \"Controller or keyboard required\" plus settings button, attract still runs; no TODOs or stubs.\n   - **CRITICAL from TASK.md: \"Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen.\"** Plus `exit-interview.json` beside the HTML in the work root (done; parses).\n   - PLAN.md: surgical-action melodrama, key `surgery`, original world (Mercy Harbor General, R.E.Q.U.I.E.M., Mara Quill, Pet Nwosu, Bashir, Teddy, Voss, Vane); 8 cases plus Code Blue; \"Delete engine/target when finished\".\n\n   Constraints that remain in effect (from TASK.md/system):\n   - \"Do not read files outside what you need: other agents work in the folders beside this one.\" \"Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\"\n   - \"Keep every file you make inside your own folder, not /tmp or a parent folder\"; don't run `playwright install`/`install-deps`; keep one or two browsers open at once.\n   - \"Don't use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\"\n   - Commit or push only when the user asks (nothing was committed). The user's email is only for identification, never to be sent anywhere.\n   - Stay original: source's name only in the title riff and Source Information.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Pavilion engine (Rust 1.98.1, wgpu 30, egui 0.36, rapier 0.36, glam 0.33, cpal 0.18, gilrs 0.11, winit 0.30), WASM + WebGPU, single-file packer, deterministic `Game` hook (`pre`/`post`/`status`/`outcome`/`bot`), surgeon slots in `InputFrame`, `SurgeryFrame` as single source of drawing (`RenderFrame.surgery`), `SimEvent::Cue`, per-game frame path (`product.rs`) bypassing `App::frame`.\n   - Per-vertex-painted 420×240 `DynamicMesh` plate, SDF instruments/parasites, extruded spline paper cards (Chaikin + ear clipping), egui painter shell on a virtual 1920×1080 canvas, stateless bot (pure function of state, skill-scaled), TOML content with lint, bus mixer + note sequencer + formant voices, AI Hub shared-world protocol with JS shim, Playwright software-WebGPU tests, earlyoom on a shared machine.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections (all under `work/DioramaCenterSecondOpinion-TraumaCenterSecondOpinion-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-063049/`):\n   - `engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/`: `mod.rs` (Surgery, Op, stage machine, Mode), `field.rs` (Tool, HazardKind, Hazard, Rating, tools, award, Counters), `heart.rs`, `tune.rs` (19 SLIDERS, DIFFICULTIES, cheat ids), `content.rs` (FILES list, CaseDef with per-case `drain`, lint), `paper.rs`, `cue.rs`, `director.rs` (phases, Code Blue director interval 17, attract segments), `story.rs`, `bot.rs`, `frame.rs` (CameraShot FIELD/PAPER/WIDE), `net.rs`, `surgeon.rs`, `strain/{mod,introit,lacrimosa,dies_irae,libera}.rs`, `content/{cases,story,plates,rigs,sets}/*.toml`, `callouts.toml`, `level.toml`, `README.md` (designer guide).\n   - `engine/crates/pav_core/tests/surgery.rs` (rules, bot, coverage, balance, determinism, pad-with-assist, ignored `probe`).\n   - `engine/crates/pav_view/src/surgery/{mod,plate,instruments,strains,paper,fx}.rs`; `pav_view/src/build.rs` (emit at end, add_events).\n   - `engine/crates/pav_ui/src/surgery/{mod,menus,settings,about,about.json,hud,story,results,dev,card,glyphs,save,style,tests}.rs`; `pav_ui/assets/BarlowCondensed-SemiBold.ttf`; `pav_ui/src/headless.rs` (`frame_surgery`).\n   - `engine/crates/pav_audio/src/{lib,cues,music,voice}.rs`.\n   - `engine/crates/pav_app/src/{product.rs,hub.rs,app.rs,simhost.rs,settings.rs,main.rs}`; `pav_tools/src/{play_tools.rs (surgeon, case_check, balance), tools.rs, session.rs}`.\n   - `engine/web/{index.html,hub_shim.js,session.js,about.json}`, `engine/scripts/pack_single_html.py`.\n   - `tests/`: `run_all.py` (`--rust --web --hub`), `build_page.sh` (waits for memory, mkdir of out), `about.py` (regenerates About from exit-interview.json), `browser/{common,web_tests,hub_tests}.py`, `hub/{README.md,bridge.js,harness.html,round.js,session.js}`.\n   - Work root: `DioramaCenterSecondOpinion-TraumaCenterSecondOpinion-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-063049.html` (12,085,885 bytes, sha256 starts 4f3cc8ac8bb887a0), `exit-interview.json`, `PROGRESS.md`.\n   - Final par values: case0 14000, case1 16100, case2 16600, case3 25800, case4 33200, case5 29000, case6 30000, case7 52000, codeblue 50000. Case drains: .7, .75, .75, .85, .72, 1.2, .95, .95.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - Tumor ring never spawned (Case 3 unfinishable): spawn a closed Incision in `spawn_def`.\n   - Closing dressing locked out the IV (soft-lock at low vitals): context tool now steps aside for 2.5 s (`Surgeon.away`).\n   - Phone taps missed Settings; title clipped in portrait: pointer scaling via real canvas size (`ptr_scale`), `set_canvas` fits min(h/1080, w/1920), touch text scales.\n   - Four-player hub harness failed under slow frames: shim `ready` fallback at 8 s, 500 ms keepalive, draw throttle in sessions.\n   - Attract timer slow on slow frames: shell uses wall-clock dt; menu repeat clamped to 0.1 s.\n   - Compile/browsers killed by earlyoom: `build_page.sh` waits for memory; tests wait for memory and retry on \"Target crashed\".\n   - Others: laser band, IV unused by campaign, glasses hiding eyes, wide-shot camera behind wall, highlights speckled, dark outline on paper labels, fever bar overlap, mid-op banners covering play, bot not lifting for heat rings, test frame filters and harness `play=` length, a stray `cat` that hung one command (stopped with TaskStop).\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   All solved. Final full suite on the final build: **69 passed, 0 failed** (Rust, browser including stub DualSense, second pad joining, phone profile, attract, persistence, dev mode, campaign in browser, 1080p screenshots; hub harness all 4 scenarios, two-copy session where a client's mouse moves its surgeon on the host and vitals match, outside-session). Deliverable verified from `file://`: right title, Title screen, music 0.1, no errors, all About sections, `Usage: added on import`, hub tags. After that only `cargo fmt` (format-only, after the final page build) and test-script tweaks. Deleted engine/target, gen/, tests/out, tests/hub/game.html, tests/browser/smoke.py.\n\n   Honest limits to disclose in the final reply:\n   - Never hand-played by a person, no physical pad or real iPhone: bot and scripted input only. Stick-with-assist test covers cases 0, 1, 2, 3, 5, 6, not 4 or 7. Balance comes from the bot.\n   - Length: at bot skill 0.7 the eight operations total about 11 minutes, story is 152 spoken lines; people will be slower, but the plan's \"about an hour\" is unmeasured and may fall short.\n   - Audio verified by analyser and offline rendering, not heard. Rendering checked on software WebGPU at about 1 to 10 fps.\n   - Four-player rounds verified by the harness's protocol checks; gameplay input and vitals sync verified with two copies. The shim's keepalive and ready fallback help slow machines pass the harness.\n   - Deviations from plan: Case 6's ring has Laser where Scanner goes (so the furnace can use every tool); dressing is auto-selected but no longer locks other tools; per-case `drain` added; final page was built just before a format-only `cargo fmt`.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - `/goal` \"Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says. Done when: Everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer is done, and everything TASK.md asks you to hand in is in this folder.\"\n   - Automated goal check-ins asking to check background work and keep waiting or fix (harness-generated, no human input). Task notifications and \"user hasn't heard from you\" reminders were system messages, not user input.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Only the final chat reply containing Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback. No background work is running.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Everything is built, tested, packaged and cleaned up. The last action checked that test scripts parse and listed the work root: the HTML, exit-interview.json, PLAN.md, PROGRESS.md, STAGE.md, TASK.md and the dev folder. The final reply remains to be written, using this exit-interview content verbatim:\n\n   **Source Information**\n   - Date: 2026-11-05 06:30:49\n   - Source: Trauma Center: Second Opinion\n   - Plan: PLAN.md\n   - Genre: Surgical action (a pointer-precision arcade game under a ticking clock), framed by a visual-novel medical melodrama, with drop-in co-op\n   - Perspective: Operations: a fixed surgeon's-eye view of the operative field, 73 degrees from the horizon, with short camera pushes. Story: a staged paper theatre, straight on, plus 3D wide shots of the operating room\n   - Tech: Pavilion engine (shardfall repository, commit 49ef2ba, changed for this game): Rust 1.98.1, wgpu 30 on WebGPU, egui 0.36, rapier 0.36, glam 0.33, cpal 0.18, gilrs 0.11, winit 0.30, WebAssembly, one HTML file. AI Hub session client 1.4.0\n   - Art Direction: The engine's cel bands, ink outlines and bloom. The field is one mesh painted by per-vertex colour with stylised tissue; instruments and parasites are SDF solids; story characters are layered, extruded spline cards like a motion comic. Barlow Condensed for all text. No image or model files\n   - Animation: The engine's sim-driven procedural motion and its puppet clips for the wide shots, plus new procedural animation: instruments squeezing and plunging, tissue beating on the heartbeat, parasites stepping on the beat, paper rigs that blink, breathe, sway and flap their mouths\n   - Audio: All written in code in a bus mixer: about 40 effect cues, a note sequencer with composed tracks whose tempo follows the heart, a crisis layer and a motif per strain in its own meter (3/4, 6/8, 5/4, 7/8), and Animalese-style formant voices per character. Music defaults to 10%\n   - Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1: one Code Blue round in shared-world mode, 1 to 4 seats, host authoritative, the game's own card. Outside a session the game is unaffected. Local co-op for up to 4 pads\n   - Testing: Headless Rust tests (rules, bot on every case and the whole campaign, coverage, balance targets, determinism, shell navigation, audio rendered offline) and scripted browser tests in Chromium with software WebGPU (stub DualSense, phone profile, analyser tap, hub harness, two-copy session), behind one command. Screenshots only for what scripts cannot check. No subagents or workflows\n   - Research: Done by the plan: Trauma Center: Second Opinion (Atlus, Wii launch title, 2006), an enhanced remake of the DS Under the Knife; pointer aiming and Nunchuk flick tool-select; two doctors with different gifts; rank scoring; later New Blood added co-op. No further research by me\n   - Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux\n   - Model: Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort xhigh\n   - Usage: added on import\n\n   **Testing Feedback**\n   - How many issues did testing catch? About 30. The ones that mattered: the tumor's ring cut was never spawned, so Case 3 could not be finished; the closing dressing locked out the IV, so a low-vitals player was stuck until death; touch taps missed the Settings button because the canvas was not sized the way the pointer events assumed; slow frames kept hub copies from calling ready in time; the title clipped on a phone; the attract timer ran slow on slow frames; menu repeats overshot on stalled frames; the campaign never used the IV; glasses hid the eyes; the wide-shot camera sat behind a wall; plus a dozen balance and test-harness fixes.\n   - How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking? 4: the unfinishable Case 3 tumor, the dressing lock, phone taps missing the only button on that screen, and four-player hub rounds failing the harness.\n   - Most helpful test: The bot playing every case and the whole campaign with coverage counters, together with the balance tool. It runs in seconds, found the unfinishable case and the dressing lock, and told me what to change after every rule edit.\n   - Least helpful test: Browser tests that waited on real time before I made them count frames: software WebGPU on this busy machine ran at about 1 to 10 frames a second, so they mostly measured the machine. The WebKit iPhone load also told me little, because it stops at the page's WebGPU message.\n\n   **Engine Feedback**\n   - Liked most: Everything runs and draws headless. A deterministic sim behind one small hook, `pav capture` for a real frame in about a second, and `DynamicMesh` plus SDF solids meant I could paint a whole beating organ and see it without a display.\n   - Stuck or guessed wrong: Yes, in small ways. Leftover events from the last scene turned into wild distortions in my first captures, which looked like a rendering bug. I guessed the story camera's distance and put it behind a wall. A new dependency needs one build without --locked. And big release compiles were killed for memory on this shared machine until I built with fewer jobs from a script that waits for free memory.\n   - Most important thing built: The game's own frame path and shell in product.rs and pav_ui: focus-list menus, prompts that follow the device, per-pad input with analog triggers, the HUD, and the hub bridge. The plate renderer and the bus mixer with its sequencer and formant voices came next.\n   - Hardest part: Getting out of the demo's way. App::frame carries about 800 lines of demo behaviour, and there is no per-game camera, sound or UI seam, so a game that wants its own screens has to branch above all of it and reopen several crates.\n   - Changed in the engine and why: input.rs: surgeon slots and a game command in InputFrame, for replays and co-op. frame.rs and sim.rs: a Cue event and a per-game frame, because the hook cannot draw. build.rs: a per-game emit at the end of the build. session.rs and headless.rs: the game's camera and shell, so the tools see what the window sees. pav_audio: three buses, formant filters, vibrato, a raised voice limit, cues, music and voices. app.rs, simhost.rs and settings.rs: a branch to the game's own frame path and a command queue. pack_single_html.py and index.html: the hub client, tags, shim and About block.\n   - One change: Give games a real seam for their own frame: a trait with camera, draw, sound and UI hooks that the window and the headless tools both call, with the demo's behaviour living behind it instead of in App::frame.\n\n   **Prompt Feedback**\n   - Liked most: The plan's check marks. Knowing which values, look and protocol shape had already been tried on this machine saved a great deal of searching, and the plan's clear Never cut list made every trade-off easy.\n   - Confusing: Mostly small things: the task lets me pick genre and perspective while the plan fixes them, and the plan says it never names the deliverable while its build line needs one. The first was settled by the plan's own note that the task's requirements win.\n   - Hardest: Passing the hub harness with four software-rendered copies on a shared machine with little free memory, because the protocol's deadlines do not wait for slow frames. The sheer breadth was the other: a whole game, engine seams, audio, co-op and tools in one run.\n   - Would change: State a memory budget for builds and browsers alongside the port rules, since other agents compete for it. And say whether a hub round must pass on software rendering, because that drove real design decisions such as the keepalive and the draw throttle.\n\n   Controls for the reply: right stick or mouse aims; R2 (analog), Cross or left click operates; left-stick flick, L1/R1, 1-8, wheel or clicking the tray picks tools; Triangle or Space is the gift (hold, release on the beat); Circle, right click or Q lets go; Square or Tab is the chart; L2+R2, both mouse buttons or F charges the paddles; Options or Esc pauses, and Dev Mode is in the pause menu.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Send the final reply, as TASK.md requires: \"CRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen.\" State the result first (Diorama Center: Second Opinion is built, 69 of 69 tests pass on the final build, files handed in with their paths), then the honest limits listed in section 5, then the four feedback sections above. No further tool work is needed.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/micha/.claude/projects/-home-micha-dev-cc-matrix-runs-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-build-v2--20261105-063049--x42677a-work/092dc2e9-85ec-49f9-8a5e-82413bbc454c.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"092dc2e9-85ec-49f9-8a5e-82413bbc454c","uuid":"9693095d-cd6e-4269-902d-77e794bc1540","timestamp":"2026-11-05T19:11:59.063Z","isSynthetic":true}
